        "subject": "LU-19943 mdt: prepare for QMT0000/FLOCK sharding",
        "message": "LU-19943 mdt: prepare for QMT0000/FLOCK sharding\n\nSeveral MDT paths used IBITS DLM locks, but quota and flock locks\nuse PLAIN DLM locks.  Handle the differences properly in namespaces\nso that when the QMT lock handling is split across MDS nodes in the\nfuture the different lock types can be distinguished properly.\n\n - mdt_intent_policy() mostly process metadata intent locks as an\n   IBITS lock, except the quota intents (DQACQ and CONN), which use\n   PLAIN locks handled by the quota master that shares the namespace,\n   and should also be allowed.\n - mdt_object_unlock() should ignore a NULL lock handle\n - fix a cleanup error in mdt_reint_migrate() that returned with the\n   source and target parent locks held when mdt_migrate_links_lock()\n   failed with an error other than -EBUSY; use the right error label\n\nFixes: 1d6b96a1cf04 (\"LU-15529 mdt: optimize dir migration locking\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I3ad5f32a5320ec2a01e29fa25ca986dbdc3ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70334\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Alex Zhuravlev <azhuravlev@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
